BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Margaret Jacobs Cameron Visiting Artist Lecture
DTSTART:20261105T163000
DTEND:20261105T173000
DTSTAMP:20261105T185042Z
UID:41e3e8ca20eea8e68238aa29f03815@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Margaret Jacobs is a Kanien’kehá:ka (Mohawk) metalsmith\, w
 ho creates fabricated steel sculpture that showcase and explore kinships t
 o botanicals and the natural world as well as values systems that we hold 
 as humans. Margaret’s work explores the lines of contemporary craft and 
 art objects alongside Indigenous narratives (as an enrolled member of the 
 Akwesasne Mohawk Nation) as well as historical and personal narratives. By
  melding historical narratives with cultural and personal narratives\, com
 plex layers of storytelling are developed in her work. Margaret will give 
 a talk about her artistic practice\, in tandem with her current exhibition
  in the Johnson Exhibition Gallery.\n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Johnson Memorial Building Classroom 204\, 78 Chateau Road
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/margaret-j
 acobs-cameron-visiting-artist-lecture-27-10-2026-12-25-14
END:VEVENT
