BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fall 2026 Musical Come From Away at SUNY Plattsburgh
DTSTART:20261108T193000
DTEND:20261109T140000
DTSTAMP:20261105T185042Z
UID:e9024c2b0fe976fb5f07e7375aded0@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:The SUNY Plattsburgh Departments of Music and Theatre will be 
 presenting a Fall 2026 Musical — Come from Away by Irene Sankoff and Dav
 id Hein — Thursday\, November 5 to Sunday\, November 8\, 2026. Come From
  Away is a critically acclaimed and award-winning musical by Irene Sankoff
  and David Hein. The show is based on the true story when the isolated com
 munity of Gander\, Newfoundland\, played host to the world. What started a
 s an average day in a small town turned into an international sleepover\, 
 when 38 planes\, carrying thousands of people from around the globe\, were
  diverted to Gander’s airstrip on September 11\, 2001. Undaunted by cult
 ure clashes and language barriers\, the people of Gander cheered the stran
 ded travelers with music\, an open bar\, and the recognition that we’re 
 all part of a global family. (MTIshows.com} Come From Away is an uplifting
  reminder of humanity’s ability to come together\, no matter what the ci
 rcumstances. This production has musical direction by Pamela Lavin\, chore
 ography by Mireena Fleury\, stage direction by Shawna Mefferd Kelty\, and 
 is being conducted by Daniel Gordon. Come from Away will be performed in t
 he Hartman Theatre within the John Myers Building on November 5\, 6 and 7 
 at 7:30 p.m.\, and November 8 at 2 p.m. General Admission for the performa
 nce is $20\, and Student Association members admission is $10. Tickets are
  on sale now and can be bought online at https://campusgroups.plattsburgh.
 edu/musthe/events/\, or at the cash only box office an hour before the per
 formances. Artist Group Info butc3332@plattsburgh.edu 26 Rugar Street Plat
 tsburgh \, New York 12901 5185642243 butc3332@plattsburgh.edu https://camp
 usgroups.plattsburgh.edu/musthe/events/ Submit An Event Find out what's ha
 ppening in your neck of the woods with Vermont Public's free Events newsle
 tter. Email Address * Editorial Emails Breaking News | sent occasionally T
 he Frequency | Daily News Update\, sent weekday mornings Capitol Recap | V
 ermont Legislature Wrap\, sent Fridays during the session Brave Little Sta
 te | People-Powered Journalism\, sent every other Saturday But Why | A Pod
 cast For Curious Kids\, sent every other Friday Homegoings | A righteous s
 pace for art and race\, sent bi-weekly following an episode drop Out There
  | Out There | Your monthly dose of the environment + the great outdoors\,
  sent Thursday mor Supporter Emails Membership Renewal Notices | Sent 12 m
 onths after your most recent contribution The President's Report | A lette
 r from our president exclusively for members of our Producers Circle The T
 ransmitter | A behind-the-scenes newsletter exclusively for active members
 \, sent the first Tues But Why Fan Club | Activity Newsletter exclusively 
 for active members of the But Why Fan Club\, sent Other Fundraising Emails
  | Matching challenges\, prize drawings and more\, sent periodically Audie
